      "gap": "Durrett's remark after Theorem 3.2.11 (p. 120) is general. When P(Xn = xn) = 1 with xn in an open set G and xn -> x on the boundary of G, P(Xn in G) = 1 for every n while the limit gives G probability 0; K = G^c gives the matching example for closed sets. The handbook gives only one instance, delta_{1/n} => delta_0 with G = (0,inf) and K = (-inf,0] (lines 439-442; annex 851-860). It states neither the general boundary-approach remark nor that point masses at xn converge weakly to the point mass at x whenever xn -> x. The general form is supplied only in the uninput file measure-integration-and-product-constructions-w02c-p15-004.tex.",
